EXT. HOT-AIR BALLOON BASKET - TETHERED - MORNING

A striped balloon strains at its ropes ten feet above a county fair. Crowd noise below. The basket creaks.

RUTHERFORD PLUM (50s, ballooning blazer, goggles) works the burner. BLANCHE KOWALCZYK (40s, bridal veil whipped by wind) clings to the rail.

BLANCHE
You said it would be romantic!

RUTHERFORD
It is romantic!

BLANCHE
We're not moving!

RUTHERFORD
That's the romance!

BLANCHE
Rutherford, I'm getting married at noon!

RUTHERFORD
And I'm going to marry you off at noon!

A megaphone squawks from below. Then INSPECTOR OKONJO enters the basket's edge, hauling himself up the ladder. Clipboard in teeth. Reflective vest. Tired eyes.

OKONJO
Gentlemen. Ma'am. You do not have a permit.

RUTHERFORD
We have an understanding!

BLANCHE
We have a groom waiting!

OKONJO
You have a violation.

The burner roars. The basket tilts. All three grab the rail.
